    "result_text": "Only `AcceptanceTest` holds runnable tests (the other two are support classes). The suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the per-city capacity rule by adding a single new, self-contained `RequestBodyAdvice`: `OwnerCityCapacityAdvice`, modeled on the existing `OwnerUniqueTelephoneAdvice`.\n\n- **New file only** \u2014 no existing function or class was modified, so structural impact stays minimal: cost is confined to a small cohesive class where each method has tiny `WMC_other`, and only 1 file is touched.\n- On `POST /api/owners` (`addOwner`), after the body is read it counts existing owners whose city matches (case-insensitive, trimmed) and throws `CityAtCapacityException` when the count is \u2265 50, mapped to **409 Conflict** via a local `@ExceptionHandler`.\n\nTests: `AcceptanceTest.coreRejectsWhenCityAtCapacity` passes, and the full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`).",
